t a suitability rationale explaining why Aviva meets objectives. (7) Investment pathway rejection: Report cites underperformance of investment pathways as rejection reason but provides no specific fund name, return data, or time period for the comparison. The evidence [P22] confirms the four rejection reasons stated but does not substantiate the performance claim. (8) Adviser monitoring claim: Report states moving to Aviva enables 'active adviser monitoring and adjustment' vs remaining with Quilter, but no evidence compares actual monitoring or adjustment capabilities between platforms. The claim lacks substantiation. Overall, the report satisfies the structural requirement (alternatives are presented with stated reasons) but fails to deliver client-specific economic justification. The recommendation's cost-benefit analysis is incomplete: charge savings of £208 are offset by critical yield shortfalls of 1.19%-1.26% and projected fund reductions of 12.42%, yet this trade-off is not explained to the client. The risk-alignment rationale conflicts with the report's own acknowledgment that the rejected Nest fund achieved superior returns. The rationale appears generic across all three arrangements rather than tailored to each arrangement's specific case for switching or retaining.","citations":[{"passageId":"P4","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I_RecommendationsAndAdvice","quote":"I recommend placing these funds into a new plan on the Aviva platform for the following reasons: The receiving scheme has a lower overall cost structure compared to the Quilter plan. We have negotiated a reduced platform charges of 0.19%, compared to the Quilter charges of 0.27%, representing a savings of £208 per annum, based on the estimated fund value.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I_RecommendationsAndAdvice","quote":"You mentioned during our meeting that you had no ties or preference to leave the funds with Quilter.","cel