{"groupId":"CHK-007","requirement":"[G7.7] Alternatives provide better cost or benefit to the client — Does the Suitability Report disclose all material charges relevant to the recommendation, including applicable initial, ongoing, product, platform, investment and transaction costs, and where higher costs arise, does the report clearly explain the benefits expected to be received by the client in exchange for those costs and are they supported by and consistent with the evidence provided?","reportSays":"The report asserts two cost comparisons: (1) a £19.15 per annum increase in charges when switching Nest to Aviva, described as 'a relatively small increase of £19.15 per annum, based on the current values'; (2) a -£275.37 saving (or -0.59%) when switching True Potential to Aviva. The report states platform charges reduce from 0.40% (True Potential) to 0.21% (Aviva), saving £88.68, and fund charges reduce from 0.58% to 0.20%, saving £177.35. For Quilter, the report states a platform charge reduction from 0.27% to 0.19%, saving £208 per annum. The report provides benefits justification: lower cost structure, active monitoring, online access, flexible retirement options, and wider fund range. Initial advice fee of 3% is stated but the extracted inconsistency shows £9,838.36 claimed as 3% of £67,945.44 (actual 3% would be £2,038.36, making the stated figure 14.49% instead). The report recommends switching all three existing arrangements to Aviva.","fileSays":"Provider illustration documents [P1], [P2], [P3], [P4] contain Critical Yield and Reduction in Yield analyses. For True Potential (IAC only, ex existing OAC) [P3]: Existing Scheme projected fund at 2.94% growth = £48,651; Aviva projected = £47,300, a reduction of 1.35% (Reduction in Yield 0.3%). For Nest (ex existing OAC) [P1]: Existing Scheme at 2.94% growth = £85,961; Aviva Pension Portfolio = £73,200, a reduction of 14.75% (Reduction in Yield 1%). For Quilter/SELECTAPENSION (All charges ex existing OAC) [P1]: no direct comparison table shown. The suitability report [P8], [P9] states Quilter platform charges 0.27% vs Aviva 0.19% (saving £208), True Potential 0.40% vs Aviva 0.21% (saving £88.68 stated in [P9]), and fund charges True Potential 0.58% vs Aviva 0.20% (saving £177.35). Death benefit analysis [P5], [P6] shows day-one transfer losses: True Potential £1,400 loss (£46,672.80 to £45,272.62), Nest loss of £638.18 (£21,272.64 to £20,634.46). The provider illustrations show Critical Yield requirements ranging from 0.09% to 0.53% above assumed growth for Aviva, and Reduction in Yield of 0.3% to 1.6% depending on scenario.","discrepancies":["Report states £19.15 per annum increase for Nest switch; derived figure from computed charge arithmetic (19.15 at 0.09% implies fund value £21,277.78, matching Nest current value) but provider illustration [P1] shows Nest switching to Aviva results in 14.75% reduction in fund value at 2.94% growth (£85,961 existing vs £73,200 Aviva), representing far greater cost impact than £19.15 per annum suggests.","Report states -£275.37 saving (-0.59%) for True Potential switch; provider illustration [P3] shows True Potential existing scheme projects to £48,651 at 2.94% growth vs Aviva £47,300, a reduction of 1.35% or approximately -£1,351 (not -£275.37). The -£275.37 figure does not reconcile to the Critical Yield projection.","Report claims 3% initial advice fee on £67,945.44 transfer value, stated as £9,838.36; 3% of £67,945.44 = £2,038.36. The stated £9,838.36 is 14.49% of transfer value, not 3%. Internal inconsistency within report's own figures.","Report states True Potential platform charges 0.40% but extracted data notes this was 0.98% in 'Pension Switch Charges Only Assessment' (including 0.50% advice charge and 0.58% fund charges). Report later correctly distinguishes ongoing fund charges 0.58% separately, but initial statement of 0.40% platform charge is incomplete representation of total costs.","Report describes Nest switch as beneficial for 'lower cost structure' but provider illustration [P1] shows Critical Yield requirement of 1% (Reduction in Yield 1%) and actual projected shortfall of £12,761 at 2.94% growth (£85,961 vs £73,200). This contradicts the 'lower cost' narrative.","Report describes True Potential switch benefits including 'lower overall cost structure' and lists fund charge savings of £177.35, yet provider illustration [P3] shows projected fund at retirement £1,351 lower with Aviva (£47,300 vs £48,651), demonstrating costs do not translate to benefit."],"comparisonPerformed":false,"missingInputs":["Basis of the -£275.37 saving claim: report does not state whether this is one-off, annual, or cumulative; it does not reconcile to any figure in provider illustrations.","Basis of the £19.15 per annum increase: while derived arithmetic implies this is Nest's annual charge difference, the provider illustration shows 14.75% fund reduction on switch, creating unexplained disconnect between annual charge and total cost of recommendation.","Aggregated all-in cost comparison: report lists individual cost reductions (£208 for Quilter, £88.68 and £177.35 for True Potential) but never totals cumulative cost or savings across all three arrangements being switched.","Adviser fee structure: report states 3% initial advice fee but does not reconcile this to client agreement or state whether this applies to all three arrangements or one only.","Alternative costs not presented: report recommends against leaving funds in place or switching only funds within existing arrangements, but does not present cost comparison for these alternatives, only narrative justification.","Day-one transfer losses: report does not disclose or aggregate the death benefit reductions shown in provider illustrations (True Potential -£1,400, Nest -£638.18), which represent immediate costs of transfer."],"analysis":"The requirement asks whether the report discloses all material charges, explains benefits for higher costs, and whether those benefits are supported by and consistent with evidence. Three material failures emerge: (1) ARITHMETIC FAILURE: The initial advice fee stated as 3% of £67,945.44 calculates to £2,038.36, not £9,838.36 as claimed. The stated amount is 14.49% of transfer value. This is an arithmetically impossible charge figure against the stated basis. (2) RECONCILIATION FAILURE: For True Potential, the report claims a -£275.37 saving (-0.59%), but the provider illustration [P3] projects existing scheme at £48,651 (2.94% growth) vs Aviva at £47,300, a shortfall of £1,351 or -2.77%. The -£275.37 figure does not reconcile to any line in the evidence and is unsupported. (3) BENEFIT CLAIM CONTRADICTED BY EVIDENCE: The report recommends switching Nest stating 'lower cost structure' benefits, yet provider illustration [P1] shows projected fund reduction of 14.75% (£85,961 to £73,200) at 2.94% growth and a Reduction in Yield of 1.0%. The annual charge difference of £19.15 cannot explain a 14.75% fund reduction. Similarly, for True Potential, the report claims lower costs justify the switch, but evidence shows the recommended Aviva portfolio projecting £1,351 less at retirement than remaining in True Potential at the same growth assumption. (4) INCOMPLETE AGGREGATION: The report lists individual charge reductions for each arrangement (Quilter £208, True Potential £88.68 + £177.35 = £266.03 total) but never aggregates total cost savings across all three arrangements or shows cumulative impact. The decision logic requires 'cumulative impact and a cost comparison present and arithmetically sound'. (5) SILENT OMISSION OF DAY-ONE COSTS: Provider illustrations [P5], [P6] show death benefit reductions (True Potential -£1,400, Nest -£638.18) occurring on day of transfer. These are material costs never disclosed in the suitability report and not aggregated with ongoing charge impacts. (6) UNRECONCILED BASIS: The report's platform charge for True Potential is stated initially in recommendations as 0.40%, but the extracted metadata notes this rose to 0.98% when including the 0.50% ongoing advice charge. The report does later separate out fund charges (0.58%) but does not clearly disclose to the client what the total ongoing cost will be with advice. (7) NO ALTERNATIVE COST ANALYSIS: The report rejects alternatives (leave in place, switch funds only) but provides no cost figures for these alternatives to support why switching to Aviva is better value. The guard states 'A cheaper option rejected for evidenced non-cost reasons is a valid outcome', but the report rejects alternatives using cost arguments ('lower overall cost structure') without presenting comparative cost evidence. The vulnerability overlay: the extracted data notes no specific vulnerability characteristics are recorded for this client. The ambiguity about retirement income objective (£25,000-£30,000) and retirement expenditure (£2,000 vs £2,986) does not appear to affect the charges analysis directly, as charges are stated in absolute terms and percentages independent of income assumptions. However, if retirement income is lower than assumed, the impact of charges on adequacy of outcome would be proportionally higher; this is not addressed. Overall: evidence is INCOMPLETE, figures are NOT ARITHMETICALLY SOUND (initial advice fee), comparative claims are CONTRADICTED BY PROVIDER ILLUSTRATIONS (Nest and True Potential both show fund reductions despite 'lower cost' claim), and NO AGGREGATED ALL-IN COST is presented.","citations":[{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I_RecommendationsAndAdvice","quote":"The platform charges with Aviva are 0.21% compared to the True Potential platform charges of 0.40%, this represents a saving of 0.19% or £88.68 based on the current value of the fund.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I_RecommendationsAndAdvice","quote":"The receiving scheme has a lower overall cost structure compared to the Quilter plan. We have negotiated a reduced platform charges of 0.19%, compared to the Quilter charges of 0.27%, representing a savings of £208 per annum, based on the estimated fund value.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I_RecommendationsAndAdvice","quote":"The ongoing fund charges are higher in the existing contract at 0.58% compared with 0.20% within the new plan, representing an annual saving of £177.35 based on the current value of the pension (excluding advice charges).","cells":null},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G_ProviderIllustration","quote":null,"cells":["Existing Scheme","£85,961","Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£73,200","The effect this will have on the fund if moved to Aviva","-14.75%","Reduction in Yield if moved to Aviva","1.0%"]},{"passageId":"P3","source":"Annes M SAP no charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G_ProviderIllustration","quote":null,"cells":["Existing Scheme","£48,651","Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£47,300","The effect this will have on the fund if moved to Aviva","-2.68%","Reduction in Yield if moved to Aviva","0.4%"]},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Annes M SAP IAC only ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G_ProviderIllustration","quote":null,"cells":["True Potential Personal Pension","£46,672.80","The day one effect of transfer","-£1,400"]},{"passageId":"P6","source":"Annes M SAP IAC only ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G_ProviderIllustration","quote":null,"cells":["nest Personal Pension","£21,272.64","Aviva - Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£20,634.46"]},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I_RecommendationsAndAdvice","quote":"this represents a relatively small increase of £19.15 per annum, based on the current values","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Data inconsistency","Disclosure shortfall","Weak justification"],"severity":"High","outcome":"Potentia