t provider illustrations use different bases: the SAP illustrations show fund charges net of all costs (e.g., P1 shows Aviva weighted average fund ongoing cost 0.2154%), while the report rounds this to 0.20% in its summary. This is a minor rounding difference (0.2154% vs 0.20%) and is typical of reports, but it should be disclosed if material to conclusions. Overall, the comparison is performed and figures are largely arithmetically sound when checked against plan values, but the basis of the comparison — particularly what is and is not included in the 'existing charge' for True Potential — is stated ambiguously, and the cost increase for Nest is not explained or justified against stated benefits.","citations":[{"passageId":"P7","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"Pension Switch Charges Only Assessment. The table below shows the difference in the total recurring annual charges of the existing plan and the alternative plan that has been recommended to replace it in both percentage and monetary terms. True Potential 0.98%. Impact of Recommended Alternative -0.59% Nest 0.30%. Impact of Recommended Alternative +0.09%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P12","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"Platform Charges 0.40%; Ongoing Advice charge 0.50%; Weighted Average Fund Management Charges 0.58%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"The platform charges with Aviva are 0.21% compared to the True Potential platform charges of 0.40%, this represents a saving of 0.19% or £88.68 based on the current value of the fund. The ongoing fund charges are higher in the existing contract at 0.58% compared with 0.20% within the new plan, representing an annual saving of £177.35 based on the current value of the pension (excluding advice charges).","cells":null},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":"HSBC Global Strategy Dynam