e value. The report provides one illustration of projected fund at proposed age 87 under mid growth (2.94%): £106,000 in real terms.","fileSays":"The evidence files (SAP reports [P1], [P2], [P4], [P7], [P17], [P18], [P19], [P22]) show: (1) True Potential fund value £46,672.80, projected at 2.94% growth to age 87: £85,961 (existing); switching to Aviva: £73,200, representing -14.75% effect, requiring 3.46% (vs 2.94% assumed, +0.52% outperformance needed); (2) Nest fund value £21,272.64, projected at 2.94% to age 87: £48,651 (existing); switching to Aviva: £33,400, representing -14.75% effect, requiring 4.17% (vs 2.94% assumed, +1.23% outperformance needed); (3) Combined figures show total existing arrangements £327,945.44 (all three plans), total Aviva projected £106,000 at age 89 at 2.94% from combined transfer value of £67,945.44 (True Potential + Nest only); (4) Day-one transfer loss True Potential: £1,400 (from £46,672.80 to £45,272.62 [P12]); day-one transfer loss Nest: £638 (from £21,272.64 to £20,634.46 [P1]); (5) Platform charges stated as 0.19% Aviva vs 0.40% True Potential or 0.27% Quilter; (6) Fund ongoing charges: Aviva recommended funds 0.20-0.21% combined ([P1], [P8], [P17]); True Potential existing 0.58%; Nest existing 0.30% ([P7]); (7) Performance over 5 years: Aviva Multi-Asset Plus IV 2: 54.09% ([P5]); HSBC Global Strategy Dynamic: not explicitly stated in 5-year form but shown in research; Vanguard 80% Equity: shown in research; comparison tables show Nest Higher Risk outperformed at 47.84% cumulative ([P2], [P4]); (8) Risk profile: Nest is risk 8, True Potential is not rated, Aviva recommended funds are risk 7; (9) Critical Yield analysis ([P2], [P4]) shows required outperformance of 0.52% p.a. for True Potential switch and 1.23% p.a. for Nest switch at 2.94% growth; (10) The report [P17], [P18] discloses: 'annual recurring charges assume no investment growth' and transaction costs excluded 'as these are variable'; (11) Product literature [P11], [