mployed with the same company', but [P9] states 'Melanie has now stopped working through self employment...she decided to cut ties with it all', which indicates she ceased self-employment rather than being currently self-employed. The tense and status are misaligned between report and evidence."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":["No formal vulnerability assessment methodology or scoring tool is evident in the file to corroborate how the 'Possible' designation was determined.","No documented assessment of support needs specific to the vulnerabilities is present; while estate planning and power of attorney are mentioned, no explicit support plan addressing the divorce, employment transition, or inheritance impact is recorded.","No documented assessment of whether the client's capacity or comprehension has been reviewed in light of these vulnerabilities.","Communication preferences and accessible format requirements are not documented beyond the generic statement in [P19] that reasonable adjustments are available on request."],"analysis":"The three vulnerabilities recorded in the report are all corroborated by evidence in the file. The divorce is confirmed across multiple meeting summaries and fact find documents. The employment change is documented in [P9] and [P11]. The inheritance expectation is documented in [P4] and [P9]. However, material discrepancies exist in the detail: the inheritance value differs significantly (£350,000 in report vs £150,000 in fact find vs £1.4m property value in meeting summary), and the employment status description in the report (currently self-employed) does not match the evidence ([P9] states she has stopped self-employment). The report's characterisation of divorce and employment change as 'Actual' and inheritance as 'Intended' is appropriate given the evidence, though the mixing of assertion statuses suggests the vulnerability assessment may not have been conducted with consistent methodology. The report does not explicitly acknowledge or discuss how these vulnerabilities affect support needs, communication adjustments, or suitability considerations — it records the characteristics but does not articulate how they have shaped the recommendation or what adjustments have been made. The file contains evidence of estate planning activity (will revision, power of attorney appointment to daughters documented in [P4]), and [P19] confirms reasonable adjustments are available, but no specific adjustments or support measures tailored to these vulnerabilities are documented in relation to this particular advice. The file therefore supports that vulnerabilities exist and have been identified, but does not clearly demonstrate that the report's handling of them — in terms of stated support needs, communication preferences, or duty of care measures — is fully supported or consistently applied throughout the advice.","citations":[{"passageId":"P8","source":"Meeting Summary with Jack Davidson.md","category":"C","quote":"You are currently in the process of managing your financial affairs following your recent divorce. Your proactive approach to addressing these financial matters indicates your commitment to securing your financial future.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P6","source":"Meeting Summary with Jack Davidson.md","category":"C","quote":"The process necessitates obtaining a letter of authority, which must be signed by your ex-husband, Paul Annis, to access the details of your quarter funds.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Fact Find (1).md","category":"B","quote":"Melanie has now stopped working through self employment, she was getting frustrated through work and with disagreements with her boss she decided to cut ties with it all. She will look to return to part time work in the new year as she has some holidays already booked in for August & September.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P11","source":"Meeting Summary.md","category":"C","quote":"At 55, Melanie is considering accessing her pension benefits to support herself financially during a transitional phase, with plans to return to work potentially in January. The meeting aimed to explore options for replacing her lost income, managing her expenses, and ensuring tax efficiency while considering her future financial needs.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Meeting Summary with Jack.md","category":"C","quote":"you are considering the implications of your potential inheritance from your late mother's property, valued at approximately £1.4 million. Although the timeline for receiving your share is uncertain due to ongoing legal proceedings, you are mindful of how this inheritance could impact your estate planning. You are actively engaged in updating your estate planning following your divorce...appointing your two daughters as your power of attorneys.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Fact Find (1).md","category":"B","quote":"Potential Inheritance of...£150,000.00...proceedings Estimated to be in 2-3 years time, maybe sooner","cells":null},{"passageId":"P12","source":"Meeting Summary.md","category":"C","quote":"Melanie's background as an accountant and her recent life changes...her desire to enjoy life after losing her mother, who suffered from Parkinson's and dementia.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P19","source":"TFAS Wealth Client Agreement.md","category":"A","quote":"Should you require us to make a reasonable adjustment in providing the advisory services to you, please speak to your financial adviser. Examples of reasonable adjustments may be the provision of a large print format pdf or documents provided in braille.","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Data inconsistency","Missing evidence","Disclosure shortfall"],"severity":"Moderate","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

